+# Exact joint global-band continuation for `(99,66)`
+
+Date: 2026-09-03 UTC  
+Lane: `g9966-global-band-sol56-20260903`  
+Status: computation in progress; this unsealed skeleton contains no completion marker.
+
+## 1. Result and typed scope
+
+This lane replays the charged 15-pivot endpoint and continues both common-`h3`
+branches in one declared coefficient chart.  The computations are exact over
+`Q`; a variable is eliminated in the preprocessing phase only when its
+coefficient is in `Q*`.  The localized branch parameters `rho` and `c` are
+never used as linear pivots.  Any nonlinear remainder is passed, together with
+`Zrho*rho-1` or `Zc*c-1`, to Singular only after those pivots.
+
+The completed ledger and final branch dimensions will be inserted after the
+pinned runs finish.  The result is necessarily typed `COUNTING-BOUND`: this
+lane imposes the displayed common-`h3`/major-`h2` state, the outer base-`h2`
+`D2` support preblock and successive outer `D1` rows, direct minor `F,G`
+coefficient rows, and direct Jacobian rows.  It does not invent the absent
+effective-`T2,T3` bridge identified in the charged report.  Nor does it claim
+that a finite compatible prefix is attained by a polynomial map.
+
+No result in this report is `REPRESENTATIVE`, `KELLER`, or a counterexample.
+Those labels would require recomposing a finite candidate `(F,G)` and checking
+`F_x G_y-F_y G_x == 1` coefficient by coefficient.  No such candidate has
+arisen in the bands computed here.
+
+## 2. Frozen-input custody and replay
+
+The receipt is
+`xmodel/g9966-global-band-sol56-20260903.run.v2`, with frozen basis
+`f3a999f667445abf948a5f6bbd5ffe5f8023f03b`.  I generated the checksum
+manifest mechanically from its indexed `charged_input_*_basename` and
+`charged_input_*_sha256` fields with `awk`, then ran `sha256sum -c` against
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.cNPqDa/inputs`.  All 20 entries returned `OK`; there was no
+manual transcription of any digest.  The manifest has 20 records.
+
+The frozen `first_global_band.py` was then executed as a subprocess.  Its
+stdout was byte-identical to the frozen `results.json`, whose SHA-256 is
+`f4a6f39c81e01f185bc0e6aed74e844639d21ffce3d219b6a539ee110553ae66`.
+This mechanically reproduces the charged exact-`Q` endpoint:
+
+| quantity | `delta=2` | `delta=5/2` |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| pre-outer common-`h3` dimension, centres included | 6704 | 6702 |
+| first direct pole/Jacobian prefix rank | 15 | 15 |
+| endpoint dimension | **6689** | **6687** |
+| residual equations | 0 | 0 |
+
+The continuation engine is
+`box/g9966band-20260903/band_engine.py`, pinned for accepted runs at SHA-256
+`3bd2937d75d59d59edeca1b89eba286fd2711f2d608109e7fd8971b64e059ac9`.
+Outputs made from earlier development hashes are excluded from this report.
+The independent structural outer-block driver is
+`box/g9966band-20260903/outer_major.py`, SHA-256
+`b562ff315042d6dd4de474852adfe7831730657d027bc9e9a7c6aeb37ed5a2d5`.
