+## 6. Stop condition, surviving coordinates, and next systems
+
+`{{STOP_AND_NEXT_SYSTEMS}}`
+
+The surviving names are coordinates in the declared `K2c`/outer basis.  They
+are called free only when the residual ideal is zero.  If a nonlinear residue
+appears, the report instead lists unresolved quotient generators and the
+localized Krull dimension, avoiding the false claim that a nonlinear scheme
+is an affine coordinate space.
+
+## 7. Singular and consistency controls
+
+For a nonzero residue the generated Singular ring is over characteristic zero
+with `dp` ordering on the active generators followed by the wrapper.  The
+ideal includes `Zrho*rho-1` or `Zc*c-1`.  The wrapper controls are
+
+```text
+<p,Zp-1>       -> unit ideal,
+<p-1,Zp-1>     -> nonunit ideal.
+```
+
+The raw residue's unit status is recorded rather than assumed.  A branch is
+declared `DEAD` only if the localized exact ideal is the unit ideal.  Otherwise
+the Singular codimension is subtracted from the post-`Q*` generator count.
+No modular rank is promoted to an exact result.
+
+## 8. Reproducibility and fleet decision
+
+`{{ARTIFACT_TABLE}}`
+
+The branches are independent after the shared custody and structural checks,
+so two machines can run them without communication.  Bands within one branch
+are logically sequential because each quotient is inherited by the next;
+the current self-contained driver recomputes the cumulative quotient, which
+also permits independent verification of different stages on separate
+machines at the cost of repeated work.  Modular primes may be used in parallel
+only as rank/leader scouts.  Any claimed rank, inconsistency, or dimension
+must be lifted and rechecked over `Q`; primes that divide a prospective pivot
+coefficient are discarded.
+
+For an eight-core fleet, a sensible layout is two exact branch workers, four
+independent modular scouts for the next expensive band, one exact replay
+worker, and one audit/serialization worker.  The final table reports measured
+isolated RSS per exact band, rather than multiplying the process lifetime high
+water mark.  Concurrent memory planning should use the largest observed band
+times the number of workers plus room for Singular's Gröbner basis if a
+residue appears.
+
+## 9. FALLACY-v2 audit and verdicts
+
+`{{VERDICTS}}`
+
+No cv flag is identified with a physical place or cover series.  Strict-below
+support deletion, at-level `D1` parting, and denominator shedding remain
+separate.  No exit-price assertion is introduced, so no `charge_basis` line is
+emitted.  Pole identities are used only in the two explicitly declared minor
+substitutions.  No lower bound is promoted to attainment.  The ring,
+localization, generator order, and imported coordinate-map limitation are
+stated.  Prime marks are not used ambiguously.  The absent effective-root
+bridge remains typed `OPEN[EFFECTIVE-T2-T3-BRIDGE]`.

