+# Exact joint global-band continuation for `(99,66)`
+
+Date: 2026-09-03 UTC  
+Lane: `g9966-global-band-sol56-20260903`  
+Status: computation in progress; this unsealed skeleton contains no completion marker.
+
+## 1. Result and typed scope
+
+This lane replays the charged 15-pivot endpoint and continues both common-`h3`
+branches in one declared coefficient chart.  The computations are exact over
+`Q`; a variable is eliminated in the preprocessing phase only when its
+coefficient is in `Q*`.  The localized branch parameters `rho` and `c` are
+never used as linear pivots.  Any nonzero polynomial residue is passed, together with
+`Zrho*rho-1` or `Zc*c-1`, to Singular only after those pivots.
+
+The completed ledger and final surviving-branch dimension will be inserted
+after the pinned runs finish.  Every surviving consistent branch is typed
+`COUNTING-BOUND`; a branch whose localized ideal is the unit ideal is typed
+`DEAD`.  This lane imposes the displayed common-`h3`/major-`h2` state, the
+outer base-`h2` `D2` support preblock and successive outer `D1` rows, direct
+minor `F,G` coefficient rows, and direct Jacobian rows.  It does not invent
+the absent effective-`T2,T3` bridge identified in the charged report.  Nor
+does it claim that a finite compatible prefix is attained by a polynomial
+map.
+
+No result in this report is `REPRESENTATIVE`, `KELLER`, or a counterexample.
+Those labels would require recomposing a finite candidate `(F,G)` and checking
+`F_x G_y-F_y G_x == 1` coefficient by coefficient.  No such candidate has
+arisen in the bands computed here.
+
+## 2. Frozen-input custody and replay
+
+The receipt is
+`xmodel/g9966-global-band-sol56-20260903.run.v2`, with frozen basis
+`f3a999f667445abf948a5f6bbd5ffe5f8023f03b`.  I generated the checksum
+manifest mechanically from its indexed `charged_input_*_basename` and
+`charged_input_*_sha256` fields with `awk`, then ran `sha256sum -c` against
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.cNPqDa/inputs`.  All 20 entries returned `OK`; there was no
+manual transcription of any digest.  The manifest has 20 records.
+
+The frozen `first_global_band.py` was then executed as a subprocess.  Its
+stdout was byte-identical to the frozen `results.json`, whose SHA-256 is
+`f4a6f39c81e01f185bc0e6aed74e844639d21ffce3d219b6a539ee110553ae66`.
+This mechanically reproduces the charged exact-`Q` endpoint:
+
+| quantity | `delta=2` | `delta=5/2` |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| pre-outer common-`h3` dimension, centres included | 6704 | 6702 |
+| first direct pole/Jacobian prefix rank | 15 | 15 |
+| endpoint dimension | **6689** | **6687** |
+| residual equations | 0 | 0 |
+
+The continuation engine is
+`box/g9966band-20260903/band_engine.py`, pinned for accepted runs at SHA-256
+`3bd2937d75d59d59edeca1b89eba286fd2711f2d608109e7fd8971b64e059ac9`.
+Outputs made from earlier development hashes are excluded from this report.
+The independent structural outer-block driver is
+`box/g9966band-20260903/outer_major.py`, SHA-256
+`b562ff315042d6dd4de474852adfe7831730657d027bc9e9a7c6aeb37ed5a2d5`.
+
+## 3. Declared rings, basis, and row construction
+
+The common fixed-top triangular chart is
+
+```text
+h3 = P+H,
+h2 = h3^3+C2*h3+C3,
+F  = h2^3+A2*h2+A3,
+G  = h2^2+B1*h2+B2,
+P  = y^3(y-x)^8.
+```
+
+It has 7,161 fixed-top coefficient coordinates.  The branch rings are
+
+```text
+R2  = Q[chart coordinates,u,rho,Zrho]/(Zrho*rho-1),
+R52 = Q[chart coordinates,u,v,c,Zc]/(Zc*c-1).
+```
+
+The major basis is
+
+```text
+K_Q=t^D Q(t^-1,w/t)=sum_(r,q) Qc_(r,q) t^r (w-1)^q,
+W(r,q)=3r+4q.
+```
+
+For `K2=t^33 h2(t^-1,w/t)`, the driver replaces the 106 surviving low-`q`
+outputs before the seven `h2`-`D1` equations by symbols `K2c_r_q`.  This is
+the unit-triangular coordinate change certified by the charged
+`major_tower_structure.py/json`: the unit leader is a `C3` coordinate for
+`q<=10` and a `C2` coordinate for `11<=q<=21`.  The seven displayed `D1`
+rows eliminate the charged pivots and leave 99 `K2c` directions.  The full
+original `C2,C3` inverse was not serialized by the charged driver, so this
+report treats the `K2c` basis as the declared computation basis and does not
+pretend to have mechanically rechecked an unavailable inverse map.
+
+After the common-`h3` branch map, this gives 104 inner variables for
+`delta=2` and 102 for `delta=5/2`, including their centre parameters.  The
+driver verifies the leaders
+
+```text
+delta=2:   t^9*zeta^2*(zeta+3*rho),  rho != 0;
+delta=5/2: s^21*pi*(pi^2-c),          c != 0,
+```
+
+and in the second branch imposes the charged compatibility
+`Hc_11_0=0` with `b0=0`.
+
+The four outer coefficient blocks use these finite specifications:
+
+| block | degree | `D2` boundary `W0` | `D1` normalized threshold |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| `A2` | 65 | 189 | 583 |
+| `A3` | 98 | 285 | 879 |
+| `B1` | 32 | 93 | 287 |
+| `B2` | 65 | 189 | 583 |
+
+The base-`h2` `D2` support block deletes 5,598 coordinates and leaves 1,002.
+The 15,934 literal `D1` scalar labels supported entirely on those deleted
+coordinates are recorded as redundant labels, not misreported as additional
+rank.  On the retained boundary, outer `D1` offsets `s=0,...,7` have raw-row
+counts
+
+```text
+64, 52, 40, 29, 20, 11, 6, 3
+```
+
+and exact rational ranks
+
+```text
+41, 38, 33, 25, 19, 11, 6, 3.
+```
+
+Thus the full eight-offset outer `D1` block has 225 displayed rows and rank
+176.  The larger literal system, including the already deleted support, has
+16,159 row labels and rank 5,774; the four outer blocks then retain 826
+coordinates.  These are structural ranks in the declared basis, not a claim
+that every nonredundant `h3`-adic outer-major condition absent from this lane
+has been imposed.
+
+`KF=t^99 F(t^-1,w/t)` and `KG=t^66 G(t^-1,w/t)` are built by sparse
+convolution.  Direct minor rows are obtained by the exact substitutions
+
+```text
+delta=2:   w=u*t^2+zeta*t^3,
+delta=5/2: t=s^2, w=u*s^4+v*s^6+pi*s^7.
+```
+
+The mechanically reconstructed raw finite-support label counts agree with the
+charged audit: `(F,G)=(1134,513)` for `delta=2` and `(1316,594)` for
+`delta=5/2`.  The normalized Jacobian used by the sparse engine is
+
+```text
+99*KF*(KG)_w - t*(KF)_t*(KG)_w
+-66*(KF)_w*KG + (KF)_w*t*(KG)_t.
+```
+
+An independent generic-face check reproduces
+`[x^145 y^17]J=1764*f0` and the charged complete expression at
+`[x^135 y^27]J`, including the coefficients `1104*f10+131040*g0-1656*g1`.
+
+## 4. Band convention and the requested next band
+
+The pole, Jacobian-total-degree, and major-weight filtrations are three
+different filtrations.  The frozen sources prescribe their rows but do not
+state a theorem identifying their indices.  The driver therefore records the
+following synchronization as a convention, so that no equality of flags or
+places is inferred:
+
+1. Stage 0 imposes outer `D1` offset 0, the requested next pole band, and only
+   `[x^135 y^27]J` in Jacobian degree 162.
+2. Stage 1 imposes outer offset 1, the next occupied pole exponent, and the
+   remaining degree-162 coordinates `y`-powers 28 through 162.
+3. Stage `n>=2` imposes outer offset `n` while `n<=7`, the next local pole
+   exponent, and every coefficient in Jacobian total degree `163-n`.
+
+The requested stage-0 pole exponents are exactly `(-77,-50)` for `(F,G)` in
+the `delta=2` branch and `(-181,-118)` in the `delta=5/2` branch.  Before the
+outer-major rows, a separate lossless top-fragment probe extends the frozen
+16 labeled rows as follows:
+
+| branch | new pole/J labels | new `Q*` pivots | dependent | residue | direct-prefix dimension |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| `delta=2` | 5 | **4** | 1 | 0 | **6,685** |
+| `delta=5/2` | 3 | **3** | 0 | 0 | **6,684** |
+
+For `delta=2`, the four new leaders are `A2_64_1` (Jacobian coefficient
+`1104`), `A3_95_0`, `B2_62_0`, and `B2_64_1`; the remaining `F` coordinate
+is the already-pivoted `A3_97_1`.  For `delta=5/2`, the first three of those
+leaders occur.  Jacobian-first and poles-first orders give the same ranks and
+all rows reduce to zero, so no Groebner call is needed at this direct stage.
+
+The matching outer offset has 64 raw rows, 41 rational pivots, and 23
+dependent rows.  In the declared `K2c` presentation, its 5,598-coordinate
+`D2` preblock plus offset 0 makes all 16 prior labels and all newly requested
+labels zero.  Thus the direct ranks above overlap the stronger major
+quotient and must not be added again.
+
+The final exact stage-0 accounting is:
+
+| branch | named pole/J labels | nonzero after major reduction | joint `Q*` pivots | residue | combined rank from 6704/6702 | dimension drop from banked endpoint | dimension |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| `delta=2` | 5 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 5,639 | 5,624 | **1,065** |
+| `delta=5/2` | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 5,639 | 5,624 | **1,063** |
+
+Here “combined rank” is `5598+41`.  The dimension-drop column is the direct
+subtraction `6689-1065` or `6687-1063`; it is not presented as a separately
+recomputed rank across the unserialized inverse coordinate map.  The
+cumulative driver row logs contain the 16 charged labels as well: 21 labels
+for `delta=2` and 19 for `delta=5/2`, all reducing to zero after the stronger
+major block.  No residue appears, so Singular is correctly not invoked for
+this stage (the emitted file records the zero ideal).
+
+## 5. Continuation ledger
+
+The tables use only JSON objects whose embedded `driver_sha256` equals the
+pinned digest above.  Each row states raw labels added at that stage, new
+outer rational pivots, the change in cumulative joint rational rank, exact
+Krull dimension of the displayed finite localized quotient, residue status,
+external wall time, and cumulative-stage invocation peak RSS.  The validator
+checks contiguous stage specifications, row-count identities, pivot-ledger
+shape and continuity, dimension formulas, branch identity, engine hash, and
+GNU-time inequalities.  It records artifact hashes; the separately generated
+artifact manifest is the custody list, not a claim that the validator
+recomputed every row expression or rank from an independently implemented
+engine.
+
+### `delta=2`
+
+| stage | pole `(F,G)` / J band | outer raw/rank | new pole+J labels | joint `Q*` new/cum | residue | dimension | wall | RSS KiB |
+|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| 0 | `(-77,-50)` / `J162:k27` | `64/41` | `4+1` | `0/0` | 0 | 1,065 | 116.25 s | 72,032 |
+| 1 | `(-76,-49)` / `J162:k28..162` | `52/38` | `4+135` | `9/9` | 0 | 1,018 | 210.09 s | 76,408 |
+| 2 | `(-75,-48)` / all `J161` | `40/33` | `4+162` | `9/18` | 0 | 976 | 373.02 s | 81,176 |
+| 3 | `(-74,-47)` / all `J160` | `29/25` | `6+161` | `9/27` | 0 | 942 | 364.35 s | 90,092 |
+| 4 | `(-73,-46)` / all `J159` | `20/19` | `6+160` | `8/35` | **118 constants; unit** | **DEAD** | 369.15 s | 103,336 |
+
+At stage 4, 659 joint labels give 513 initially nonzero expressions.  After
+35 cumulative `Q*` pivots, 506 are zero/dependent and every one of the 118
+remaining expressions is a nonzero integer constant.  In particular,
+
+```text
+stage4_J_d159_k35 = 6264,
+1 = (1/6264) * stage4_J_d159_k35  in Q.
+```
+
+The unlocalized reduced-residue ideal, and hence the triangularly equivalent
+stage system, is therefore already the unit ideal before `rho` is localized.
+One constant suffices; the 118 constants are not counted as 118 extra ranks.
+Singular independently checks the emitted reduced residue and returns
+dimension `-1` and basis `1`.  The stage JSON
+field named `nonlinear_residue_appears` is a legacy nonempty-residue boolean;
+the actual obstruction here is constant, not nonlinear.  There is no stage-4
+family of dimension 915: that number is only the formal generator count
+before the unit residue, and the exact final dimension is null.
+
+### `delta=5/2`
+
+`{{DELTA52_LEDGER}}`
+
+## 6. Stop condition, surviving coordinates, and next systems
+
+`{{STOP_AND_NEXT_SYSTEMS}}`
+
+The surviving names are coordinates in the declared `K2c`/outer basis.  They
+are called free only when the residual ideal is zero.  If a nonzero polynomial residue
+appears, the report instead lists unresolved quotient generators and the
+localized Krull dimension, avoiding the false claim that a nonlinear scheme
+is an affine coordinate space.
+
+## 7. Singular and consistency controls
+
+For a nonzero polynomial residue the generated Singular ring is over characteristic zero
+with `dp` ordering on the active generators followed by the wrapper.  The
+ideal includes `Zrho*rho-1` or `Zc*c-1`.  The wrapper controls are
+
+```text
+<p,Zp-1>       -> unit ideal,
+<p-1,Zp-1>     -> nonunit ideal.
+```
+
+The raw residue's unit status is recorded rather than assumed.  A branch is
+declared `DEAD` only if the localized exact ideal is the unit ideal.  Otherwise
+the Singular codimension is subtracted from the post-`Q*` generator count.
+For the `delta=2` death, an independent replay of the generated Singular file
+prints `dim=-1`, basis `1`, and controls `0,1,0`: the deliberately empty
+control and the raw constant ideal are unit, while the point control is
+nonunit.  No modular rank is promoted to an exact result.
+
+## 8. Reproducibility and fleet decision
+
+`{{ARTIFACT_TABLE}}`
+
+The branches are independent after the shared custody and structural checks,
+so two machines can run them without communication.  A stateful incremental
+implementation must process bands sequentially because each quotient is
+inherited by the next.  This self-contained driver instead recomputes every
+cumulative quotient, so distinct endpoint stages can run on separate machines
+at the cost of duplicated prefix work; the surviving branch used that mode
+after the other branch died.  A modular-prime backend is not shipped here.
+Independent primes could be added only as hypothetical rank/leader scouts;
+any claimed rank, inconsistency, or dimension would still have to be lifted
+and rechecked over `Q`, discarding primes that divide a prospective pivot.
+
+For an eight-core fleet before a branch dies, two exact branch workers, up to
+four lower-priority cumulative-stage workers, one replay worker, and one
+audit/serialization worker are independent.  After a branch dies its worker
+can take the next cumulative endpoint of the survivor.  The table reports
+isolated cumulative-invocation RSS, not marginal memory for just the newly
+added rows.  Concurrent memory planning should sum those measured peaks and
+leave separate room for Singular if a genuine polynomial residue appears.
+
+## 9. FALLACY-v2 audit and verdicts
+
+`{{VERDICTS}}`
+
+No cv flag is identified with a physical place or cover series.  Strict-below
+support deletion, at-level `D1` parting, and denominator shedding remain
+separate.  No exit-price assertion is introduced, so no `charge_basis` line is
+emitted.  The pole substitutions and branch hypotheses are imported from the
+charged section 6 prescription; this lane does not infer new geometric pole
+identities.  No lower bound is promoted to attainment.  The ring,
+localization, generator order, and imported coordinate-map limitation are
+stated.  Prime marks are not used ambiguously.  The absent effective-root
+bridge remains typed `OPEN[EFFECTIVE-T2-T3-BRIDGE]`.

