+## 3. Declared rings, basis, and row construction
+
+The common fixed-top triangular chart is
+
+```text
+h3 = P+H,
+h2 = h3^3+C2*h3+C3,
+F  = h2^3+A2*h2+A3,
+G  = h2^2+B1*h2+B2,
+P  = y^3(y-x)^8.
+```
+
+It has 7,161 fixed-top coefficient coordinates.  The branch rings are
+
+```text
+R2  = Q[chart coordinates,u,rho,Zrho]/(Zrho*rho-1),
+R52 = Q[chart coordinates,u,v,c,Zc]/(Zc*c-1).
+```
+
+The major basis is
+
+```text
+K_Q=t^D Q(t^-1,w/t)=sum_(r,q) Qc_(r,q) t^r (w-1)^q,
+W(r,q)=3r+4q.
+```
+
+For `K2=t^33 h2(t^-1,w/t)`, the driver replaces the 106 surviving low-`q`
+outputs before the seven `h2`-`D1` equations by symbols `K2c_r_q`.  This is
+the unit-triangular coordinate change certified by the charged
+`major_tower_structure.py/json`: the unit leader is a `C3` coordinate for
+`q<=10` and a `C2` coordinate for `11<=q<=21`.  The seven displayed `D1`
+rows eliminate the charged pivots and leave 99 `K2c` directions.  The full
+original `C2,C3` inverse was not serialized by the charged driver, so this
+report treats the `K2c` basis as the declared computation basis and does not
+pretend to have mechanically rechecked an unavailable inverse map.
+
+After the common-`h3` branch map, this gives 104 inner variables for
+`delta=2` and 102 for `delta=5/2`, including their centre parameters.  The
+driver verifies the leaders
+
+```text
+delta=2:   t^9*zeta^2*(zeta+3*rho),  rho != 0;
+delta=5/2: s^21*pi*(pi^2-c),          c != 0,
+```
+
+and in the second branch imposes the charged compatibility
+`Hc_11_0=0` with `b0=0`.
+
+The four outer coefficient blocks use these finite specifications:
+
+| block | degree | `D2` boundary `W0` | `D1` normalized threshold |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| `A2` | 65 | 189 | 583 |
+| `A3` | 98 | 285 | 879 |
+| `B1` | 32 | 93 | 287 |
+| `B2` | 65 | 189 | 583 |
+
+The base-`h2` `D2` support block deletes 5,598 coordinates and leaves 1,002.
+The 15,934 literal `D1` scalar labels supported entirely on those deleted
+coordinates are recorded as redundant labels, not misreported as additional
+rank.  On the retained boundary, outer `D1` offsets `s=0,...,7` have raw-row
+counts
+
+```text
+64, 52, 40, 29, 20, 11, 6, 3
+```
+
+and exact rational ranks
